+From 5ac1176eb1c7f9c7fc81ca2eff1c0ac17f106dcc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: "Brouillet, Pierrick" <pierrick.brouillet@microsoft.com>
+Date: Mon, 27 Apr 2026 10:27:59 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH 2/4] uwac: add libdecor support for Wayland window decorations
+
+Integrate libdecor as an optional dependency to provide window
+decorations (title bar, window frame) on Wayland compositors that
+don't support server-side decorations (e.g., GNOME/Mutter).
+
+When WITH_LIBDECOR=ON and libdecor-0 is found:
+- libdecor handles both SSD and CSD transparently
+- Falls back to client-side decorations when SSD is unavailable
+- Replaces manual xdg-decoration/KDE-decoration negotiation
+
+When libdecor is not available or WITH_LIBDECOR=OFF:
+- Falls back to existing SSD-only code path (unchanged behavior)
+
+Changes:
+- cmake/ConfigOptions.cmake: Add WITH_LIBDECOR option (auto-detected)
+- uwac/CMakeLists.txt: Find libdecor via pkg-config
+- uwac/libuwac/CMakeLists.txt: Conditionally link libdecor
+- uwac/templates/config.h.in: Add UWAC_HAVE_LIBDECOR define
+- uwac/libuwac/uwac-priv.h: Add libdecor fields to display/window
+- uwac/libuwac/uwac-display.c: Init/cleanup libdecor context, add
+  epoll integration for libdecor event fd
+- uwac/libuwac/uwac-window.c: Use libdecor_decorate() for window
+  creation in xdg_base path, implement configure/close/commit
+  callbacks, update title/app_id/fullscreen/destroy functions
+
+Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
+---
+ client/Wayland/wlfreerdp.c  |   4 +-
